    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48197" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεο-κόλος</span></b> , ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεηκόλος</span>
			, <i>servant of a god, priest</i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				684.1
			</span></i> (Dyme, <span class="entity">ii B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				1021.3
			</span></i> (Olympia, <span class="entity">i B.C.</span>):—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεο-κολέω</span></b> , <i>serve as a
				priest</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. Ἀσκλαπιῷ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					9(1).1066
				</span></i>
			 (<span class="entity">Amphissa</span>):—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεο-κολεύω</span></b> , ib.<i><span class="en">
				417
			</span></i> (Aetol.):</div>
